  "lines": [
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "So you're a runner. What's been going on?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Sharp pain in my right groin when I push off, it's been building for a month."},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "No doubt it's the hill sessions, I'd doubled them since January."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Does coughing or sneezing set it off?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Sneezing does, yeah."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Have you changed anything yet?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "I'm moving a bit better since I cut the hills last week, or I like to think so."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Let me have a look. Bring your knee up to your chest and across."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "That pinches deep in the groin, and squeezing my fist between your knees is sore but strong."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "I think what's going on is the hip joint getting pinched at the front, probably from the extra hill load."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "For the next three weeks, run on the flat only, no more than 5 kilometres, and stop if the pain goes above three out of ten."},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "I'm positive I can stick to that."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Good. See you next week."}
  ],
